<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss sight deposits rise to 4,326.8 million Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss sight deposits rise to 4,326.8 million Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said sight deposits rose by 724.7 million Swiss francs to 4.33 billion in the reporting period ended May 20.</p>
<p>Statement of May 20 in millions of Swiss francs:</p>
<p>					 Latest   Change since April 30</p>
<p> Sight deposits		   4,326.8	plus     724.7</p>
<p> Currency reserves	     47,722.6	plus	70.4</p>
<p> Domestic securities	    4,845.6	plus	 7.9</p>
<p> Notes in circulation	  28,657.2	minus    473.9</p>
<p> Other call deposits		235.3	plus	46.4</p>
<p> Government time deposits     1,270.7	minus    424.5</p>
<p>Borrowing at the emergency Lombard window rose by 8.3 million francs to 9.8 million in the reporting period.</p>
<p>Outstanding borrowing via the discount facility and swaps of money market certificates fell by 228.7 million francs to 1,767.4 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
